{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve copied the seed history. The relevant inputs are two ZIP archives of BUSCO single-copy ortholog alignments: `scogs_animals.zip` (241 `.mafft` alignments) and `scogs_fungi.zip` (255 `.mafft` alignments). The target is the per-alignment parsimony-informative-site percentage, then a Mann–Whitney U test between the animal and fungal percentage distributions.\n\nOrdinary Galaxy tools have a single-alignment PhyKit calculator for this exact quantity, but no ordinary tool appears to accept a ZIP/collection and emit per-file results. I’m checking whether a fresh UDT is the faithful shortest route before doing hundreds of single-alignment submissions."}}
