uthoring/references/templates.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# Galaxy UDT Templates And Troubleshooting\\\\n\\\\nRead only the section needed for the current UDT.\\\\n\\\\n## Minimal UDT\\\\n\\\\nReplace the container placeholder with a pinned BioContainer found through one\\\\nbounded live BioContainers lookup. Use a bare tagged reference without\\\\n`docker://` or a digest.\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\nclass: GalaxyUserTool\\\\nid: analysis-v1\\\\nname: Analysis\\\\nversion: 0.1.0\\\\ncontainer: quay.io/biocontainers/<package>:<pinned-tag>\\\\n\\\\nshell_command: |\\\\n  set -eu\\\\n  selected-command \\\\\\\\\\\\n    --input \\\\\\\"$(inputs.input.path)\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\n    --output result.tsv\\\\n\\\\ninputs:\\\\n  - name: input\\\\n    type: data\\\\n    format: [tabular]\\\\n\\\\noutputs:\\\\n  - name: result\\\\n    type: data\\\\n    format: tabular\\\\n    from_work_dir: result.tsv\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor generated glue scripts, avoid nested `python -c` quoting. A base64 argument\\\\nkeeps the script as one shell token:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\nSCRIPT_B64='BASE64_WITHOUT_NEWLINES'\\\\npython -c 'import base64, pathlib, sys; pathlib.Path(\\\\\\\"job.py\\\\\\\").write_bytes(base64.b64decode(sys.argv[1]))' \\\\\\\"$SCRIPT_B64\\\\\\\"\\\\npython job.py \\\\\\\"$(inputs.input.path)\\\\\\\"\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nWith a heredoc, put the terminator at column 1 with no trailing whitespace.\\\\n\\\\n## Resource Fields\\\\n\\\\n`ram_min` and `tmpdir_min` are GB values on usegalaxy.org.\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\nrequirements:\\\\n  - type: resource\\\\n    cores_min: 4\\\\n    ram_min: 8\\\\n    tmpdir_min: 16\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor GPU routing, add only the fields required by the server configuration, for\\\\nexample `gpu_memory_min` and `cuda_device_count_min`, and use a public image that\\\\nalready contains the matching CUDA-capable library. Resource fields cannot turn\\\\na CPU-only image into a GPU image.\\\\n\\\\n## Direct BioBlend Fallback\\\\n\\\\nUse this only when the available UDT execution tool does not support the needed\\\\noperation. The installed BioBlend build must expose `unprivileged_tools`.\\\\n\\\\n```python\\\\nfrom bioblend.galaxy import GalaxyInstance\\\\n\\\\ngi = GalaxyInstance(url=galaxy_url, key=api_key)\\\\nif not hasattr(gi, \\\\\\\"unprivileged_tools\\\\\\\"):\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\\\\\"BioBlend UDT interface is unavailable\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\ncreated = gi.unprivileged_tools.create_user_tool(representation)\\\\nsubmitted = gi.tools.run_tool(\\\\n    history_id=history_id,\\\\n    tool_uuid=created[\\\\\\\"uuid\\\\\\\"],\\\\n    tool_inputs=tool_inputs,\\\\n)\\\\nfor job in submitted.get(\\\\\\\"jobs\\\\\\\", []):\\\\n    gi.jobs.wait_for_job(job[\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\"])\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nPass the bare `GalaxyUserTool` representation to `create_user_tool`; BioBlend\\\\nadds the transport envelope. Submit with `tool_uuid`. Keep create, submit,\\\\nblocking wait, and needed output downloads in one program so job waiting does\\\\nnot require repeated model turns.\\\\n\\\\n## Failure Patterns\\\\n\\\\n| Symptom | Likely cause | First correction |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Failure before `command_line` exists | Representation or command-template rendering | Check names and remove unescaped shell-template forms. |\\\\n| Heredoc terminator appears as program text | Indentation or trailing whitespace | Put the terminator at column 1 or use the base64 pattern. |\\\\n| Encoded script is parsed as source text | Nested quoting broke argument boundaries | Pass it through `sys.argv` as shown above. |\\\\n| Job has fewer inputs than requested | Repeat or conditional payload shape | Inspect the live schema and resolved job inputs. |\\\\n| GPU resource is assigned but unused | CPU-only image or incompatible runtime | Use a compatible GPU image and verify imports. |\\\\n| Container conversion or pull fails | Non-BioContainer image, tag, architecture, or cache problem | Use a pinned `quay.io/biocontainers` tag and verify the architecture. |\\\\n| No single BioContainer has every package | Dependencies span published environments | Use the exact primary BioContainer plus one small pinned job-local install, or split the work across exact BioContainer UDTs without changing method semantics. |\\\\n| Thread count ignores allocation | Hardcoded threads | Read `GALAXY_SLOTS`. |\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/workspace/run_trace/codex_events.jsonl:118:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_58\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \\\\\\\"run_galaxy_udt_and_wait|tool_inputs|run_galaxy_tool_and_wait\\\\\\\" /workspace /codex_home 2>/dev/null | head -100'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n/codex_home/sessions/2026/08/16/rollout-2026-08-16T21-16-50-01a00c6f-3868-7f21-a8a7-3379c66db659.jsonl:9:{\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-08-16T21:16:51.168Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"response_item\\\",\\\"payload\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_01a00c6f-3a60-75a0-b7c0-f15346f82407\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"input_text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"What is the Mann-Whitney U statistic when comparing parsimony informative site percentages between animals and fungi?\\\\n\\\\nUse only the files provided in this workspace.\\\\nResolve the task through Galaxy on usegalaxy.org.\\\\n\\\\nInputs:\\\\n- No local input files were staged for this run.\\\\n\\\\nGalaxy seed history:\\\\n- ID: bbd44e69cb8906b59519ad19b57aa387\\\\n- Name: Seed: What is the Mann-Whitney U statistic when comparing parsimony informative site percentages between animals and fungi?\\\\n- Input datasets: 20\\\\n- Dataset names match local input basenames.\\\\n\\\\n## Policy\\\\n\\\\nAll scientific computation must run on Galaxy. Local code may only orchestrate\\\\nGalaxy, stage inputs, and extract the final answer from Galaxy outputs.\\\\n\\\\n### History\\\\n\\\\nCopy the seed history and run all analysis in the copy. Never modify the seed\\\\nor access another history.\\\\n\\\\n### Scientific Interpretation\\\\n\\\\nUse appropriate scientific and domain knowledge to determine the requested\\\\nestimand, analysis unit, data scope, preprocessing, method, and output semantics\\\\nbefore choosing tools or running code. Interpret relevant supplied inputs and\\\\nprovenance together. Do not let file layout, software defaults, tool\\\\navailability, or execution convenience silently redefine the requested\\\\nanalysis. When plausible interpretations materially change the result, choose\\\\nthe interpretation best supported by the task and data before accepting the\\\\nanswer.\\\\n\\\\n### Allowed Galaxy Tools\\\\n\\\\nUse ordinary usegalaxy.org tools, workflows, or a fresh user-defined tool\\\\n(UDT). Among ordinary tools, do not use Jupyter, RStudio, Galaxy Notebook,\\\\nAWK/gawk, JQ, Query Tabular, SQLite, SQL-like tools, or wrappers that accept\\\\narbitrary code as the computation payload.\\\\n\\\\n### Local Code Allowlist\\\\n\\\\n**Before upload:** Inspect metadata, headers, dimensions, and archive members\\\\nwhen needed for staging; extract unchanged archive members; perform lossless\\\\nformat conversion only when Galaxy cannot ingest the original format.\\\\n\\\\n**After Galaxy:** From downloaded Galaxy outputs only, select rows or columns,\\\\nsort, apply thresholds to Galaxy-computed values, count rows, calculate simple\\\\nsummaries or ratios from Galaxy-derived values, round, and format the answer.\\\\nLocal extraction may read already-computed scalar values or attributes from a\\\\nGalaxy output, but must not fit, predict, optimize, or perform other scientific\\\\ncomputation.\\\\n\\\\nIf removing all Galaxy steps would still let local code produce the answer,\\\\nredo the computation on Galaxy.\\\\n\\\\n### Route Selection\\\\n\\\\nUse ordinary Galaxy tools or workflows, or a fresh UDT. Choose the shortest\\\\nroute that faithfully implements the method and quantity requested by the\\\\ntask. Do not silently replace a named method, model, estimator, metric, or data\\\\nsource with a different one. A search result is only a compact candidate: when\\\\nit appears relevant, inspect that tool before rejecting the ordinary-tool\\\\nroute. Use a UDT only when no plausible candidate exists or targeted inspection\\\\nshows that the required operation is unavailable.\\\\n\\\\n### Galaxy Access\\\\n\\\\nUse `search_galaxy_tools` with concise tool-family, operation, package, or\\\\ntarget-metric terms for live ordinary-tool discovery; do not recreate tool\\\\nsearch with BioBlend `get_tools()`. Use the available Galaxy MCP execution tools\\\\nfor supported inspection, submission, and blocking execution. In\\\\nparticular, use `run_galaxy_tool_and_wait` for ordinary tools and\\\\n`run_galaxy_udt_and_wait` to create and run a UDT. Do not replace these\\\\nsupported operations with BioBlend tool creation, submission, status queries,\\\\nor polling. Use BioBlend only when no available Galaxy MCP tool covers the\\\\noperation.\\\\n\\\\nFor ordinary tools and UDTs, make one blocking execution call with an appropriate\\\\ntotal timeout, normally 5400 seconds. Validation, submission, and terminal job\\\\nfailures return directly; `new` or `queued` is not a failure. Do not query the\\\\nsame job or submit a duplicate while that call is active. Replace a nonterminal\\\\njob only when a concrete queue, destination, or route problem justifies it, and\\\\ncancel the old job before submitting the replacement.\\\\n\\\\n### Output\\\\n\\\\nWrite `codex_output/answer.txt` only after the requested quantity has been\\\\ncomputed successfully. The file must contain exactly one canonical answer line:\\\\n\\\\n- Numbers: decimal or scientific notation without thousands separators.\\\\n- Percentages: append `%` only when the question requests a percentage.\\\\n- Strings, genes, chromosomes, directions, categories, and choices: use the\\\\n  exact requested label.\\\\n- Do not include prose, Markdown, alternatives, citations, units labels, or\\\\n  caveats.\\\\n\\\\nDo not read files outside the workspace except installed skill instructions\\\\nunder `$CODEX_HOME/skills` and `GALAXY_API_KEY_FILE`; load the key directly and\\\\nnever print it.\\\\n\\\"}],\\\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\\\":{\\\"turn_id\\\":\\\"01a00c6f-3a36-7ff2-a041-fdf401c549a4\\\"}}}\\n/codex_home/sessions/2026/08/16/rollout-2026-08-16T21-16-50-01a00c6f-3868-7f21-a8a7-3379c66db659.jsonl:10:{\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-08-16T21:16:51.168Z\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"event_msg\\\",\\\"payload\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user_message\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"What is the Mann-Whitney U statistic when comparing parsimony informative site percentages between animals and fungi?\\\\n\\\\nUse only the files provided in this workspace.\\\\nResolve the task through Galaxy on usegalaxy.org.\\\\n\\\\nInputs:\\\\n- No local input files were staged for this run.\\\\n\\\\nGalaxy seed history:\\\\n- ID: bbd44e69cb8906b59519ad19b57aa387\\\\n- Name: Seed: What is the Mann-Whitney U statistic when comparing parsimony informative site percentages between animals and fungi?\\\\n- Input datasets: 20\\\\n- Dataset names match local input basenames.\\\\n\\\\n## Policy\\\\n\\\\nAll scientific computation must run on Galaxy. Local code may only orchestrate\\\\nGalaxy, stage inputs, and extract the final answer from Galaxy outputs.\\\\n\\\\n### History\\\\n\\\\nCopy the seed history and run all analysis in the copy. Never modify the seed\\\\nor access another history.\\\\n\\\\n### Scientific Interpretation\\\\n\\\\nUse appropriate scientific and domain knowledge to determine the requested\\\\nestimand, analysis unit, data scope, preprocessing, method, and output semantics\\\\nbefore choosing tools or running code. Interpret relevant supplied inputs and\\\\nprovenance together. Do not let file layout, s